{"content":[{"c":["DEBORAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name of two OT women. The word in Hebrew means “honeybee” (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.118.12","r":"Ps.118.12","rawR":"Ps.118.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.118.12","value":"Ps.118.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 118:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.7.18","r":"Isa.7.18","rawR":"Isa.7.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.7.18","value":"Isa.7.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 7:18"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Rebekah’s nurse (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.35.8","r":"Gen.35.8","rawR":"Gen.35.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.35.8","value":"Gen.35.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 35:8"},"). Deborah died as she was traveling to Bethel with her master Jacob’s household. She was buried in a spot remembered as Allon-bacuth (“the oak of weeping”), indicating that she had been well loved. She was probably Rebekah’s longtime companion (see ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.24.59-61","r":"Gen.24.59-61","rawR":"Gen.24.59-61","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.24.59-61","value":"Gen.24.59-61"}],"t":"ref","v":"24:59-61"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-space","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Prophetess and judge (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.4.1-5.31","r":"Judg.4.1-5.31","rawR":"Judg.4.1-5.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.4.1-5.31","value":"Judg.4.1-5.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 4–5"},"). Deborah’s position as a prophetess, indicating that her message was from God, is not unique in the Bible, but it was unusual. Other prophetesses included Miriam (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.15.20","r":"Exod.15.20","rawR":"Exod.15.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.15.20","value":"Exod.15.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 15:20"},"), Huldah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.22.14","r":"2Kgs.22.14","rawR":"2Kgs.22.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.22.14","value":"2Kgs.22.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 22:14"},"), and Anna (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.2.36","r":"Luke.2.36","rawR":"Luke.2.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.2.36","value":"Luke.2.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 2:36"},"). Deborah was unique in that only she is said to have “judged Israel” ",{"c":["before"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," the major event that marks her narrative (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.4.4","r":"Judg.4.4","rawR":"Judg.4.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.4.4","value":"Judg.4.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 4:4"},"). Her husband, Lappidoth, is otherwise unknown."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["Deborah, heralded as a “mother in Israel” (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.5.7","r":"Judg.5.7","rawR":"Judg.5.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.5.7","value":"Judg.5.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 5:7"},"), remained in one location and the people came to her for guidance. Evidently over 200 years later, when the book of Judges was compiled, a giant palm tree still marked the spot. Though residing within the boundary of Benjamin (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.4.5","r":"Judg.4.5","rawR":"Judg.4.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.4.5","value":"Judg.4.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 4:5"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.16.2","r":"Josh.16.2","rawR":"Josh.16.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.16.2","value":"Josh.16.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 16:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.18.13","r":"Josh.18.13","rawR":"Josh.18.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.18.13","value":"Josh.18.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"18:13"},"), Deborah was probably from the tribe of Ephraim, the most prominent tribe of northern Israel. Some scholars, however, place her in the tribe of Issachar (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.5.14-15","r":"Judg.5.14-15","rawR":"Judg.5.14-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.5.14-15","value":"Judg.5.14-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 5:14-15"},"). At that early time, the tribes were loosely organized and did not always occupy the territory they had been allotted."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["Under Deborah’s inspired leadership, the poorly equipped Israelites defeated the Canaanites in the plain of Esdraelon (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.4.15","r":"Judg.4.15","rawR":"Judg.4.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.4.15","value":"Judg.4.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 4:15"},"); flooding of the Kishon River evidently interfered with the enemy’s impressive chariotry (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.5.21-22","r":"Judg.5.21-22","rawR":"Judg.5.21-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.5.21-22","value":"Judg.5.21-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:21-22"},"). The Canaanites retreated to the north, perhaps to Taanach near Megiddo (v ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.5.19","r":"Judg.5.19","rawR":"Judg.5.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.5.19","value":"Judg.5.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"19"},"), and never reappeared as an enemy within Israel. The Song of Deborah (ch ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.5.1-31","r":"Judg.5.1-31","rawR":"Judg.5.1-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.5.1-31","value":"Judg.5.1-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"5"},") is a poetic version of the prose narrative in ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.4.1-24","r":"Judg.4.1-24","rawR":"Judg.4.1-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.4.1-24","value":"Judg.4.1-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Judges 4"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Barak_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Barak_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Barak_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Barak"},"; ",{"href":"?item=DeborahSongof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"DeborahSongof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"DeborahSongof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Deborah, Song of"},"; ",{"href":"?item=JudgesBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JudgesBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JudgesBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Judges, Book of"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Deborah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ps 118:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.118.12","rawQueryValue":"Ps.118.12","sourceRefExact":"Ps.118.12"},{"anchorText":"Is 7:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.7.18","rawQueryValue":"Isa.7.18","sourceRefExact":"Isa.7.18"},{"anchorText":"Gn 35:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.35.8","rawQueryValue":"Gen.35.8","sourceRefExact":"Gen.35.8"},{"anchorText":"24:59-61","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.24.59-61","rawQueryValue":"Gen.24.59-61","sourceRefExact":"Gen.24.59-61"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 4–5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.4.1-5.31","rawQueryValue":"Judg.4.1-5.31","sourceRefExact":"Judg.4.1-5.31"},{"anchorText":"Ex 15:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.15.20","rawQueryValue":"Exod.15.20","sourceRefExact":"Exod.15.20"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 22:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.22.14","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.22.14","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.22.14"},{"anchorText":"Lk 2:36","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.2.36","rawQueryValue":"Luke.2.36","sourceRefExact":"Luke.2.36"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 4:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.4.4","rawQueryValue":"Judg.4.4","sourceRefExact":"Judg.4.4"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 5:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.5.7","rawQueryValue":"Judg.5.7","sourceRefExact":"Judg.5.7"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 4:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.4.5","rawQueryValue":"Judg.4.5","sourceRefExact":"Judg.4.5"},{"anchorText":"Jos 16:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.16.2","rawQueryValue":"Josh.16.2","sourceRefExact":"Josh.16.2"},{"anchorText":"18:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.18.13","rawQueryValue":"Josh.18.13","sourceRefExact":"Josh.18.13"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 5:14-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.5.14-15","rawQueryValue":"Judg.5.14-15","sourceRefExact":"Judg.5.14-15"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 4:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.4.15","rawQueryValue":"Judg.4.15","sourceRefExact":"Judg.4.15"},{"anchorText":"5:21-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.5.21-22","rawQueryValue":"Judg.5.21-22","sourceRefExact":"Judg.5.21-22"},{"anchorText":"19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.5.19","rawQueryValue":"Judg.5.19","sourceRefExact":"Judg.5.19"},{"anchorText":"5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.5.1-31","rawQueryValue":"Judg.5.1-31","sourceRefExact":"Judg.5.1-31"},{"anchorText":"Judges 4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.4.1-24","rawQueryValue":"Judg.4.1-24","sourceRefExact":"Judg.4.1-24"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b54936e72e34d2b9bab26ad8c6a16f8e04d64c7e0c169f66e6cde6ad42f56414","sourceItemName":"Deborah","sourceItemOrder":55,"sourceMember":"Articles/D.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Deborah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Deborah","title":"Deborah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}